{
  "_comment": "NetDeflect v4 signature database. Each signature matches EXACT packet fields. category decides the mitigation strategy and whether the source is trusted (see CATEGORY_POLICY in netdeflect.py). Categories: reflection/amplification (sport-keyed responses from REAL reflectors; pattern-drop + optional null-route), reflection_tcp (unsolicited TCP replies; needs conntrack, source never blocked), dns_query/amplifier_abuse (reflection-trigger QUERIES arriving at us; forged source, per-source rate-limit), udp_flood/tcp_flood/tcp_flag/proto_flood/fragment_flood (forged source, pattern-drop, NEVER IP-blocked), syn_flood (per-source SYN rate-limit + cookies), icmp_flood (per-source rate-limit), stateful_flood (out-of-state; needs conntrack drop_invalid), botnet/scanner (REAL source, IP-blocked), game_query (connectionless UDP queries; forged, rate-limit), conn_flood (per-source connection cap; needs conntrack). Match fields: proto, sport/dport (int or list), tcp_flags (exact set, e.g. 'SYN,ACK' or 'none'; ECE/CWR honoured), tcp_flags_mask, payload_hex (+ payload_offset to anchor, payload_mask_hex for bit tests), min_len/max_len (IP datagram length), ttl_min/ttl_max, tos (DSCP byte), icmp_type/icmp_code, tcp_mss (int, [lo,hi] or 'missing'), tcp_window, tcp_reserved (int or 'nonzero'), src_ip/dst_ip (CIDR), frag ('first'|'later'|'any'). Per-rule: action (drop/allow/ratelimit/block_src/report), rate_pps, rate_bps, log, enabled, block_time, min_packets, min_percent, real_source (override).",
